# Single-page app fallback.
#
# go_router owns routes like /appointments/:id and /appointments/book, which
# exist only in the client. Without this, a hard refresh or a shared deep link
# asks Netlify for a file that was never built and gets a 404 — the app only
# ever worked when entered through /.
#
# 200 (rewrite), not 301/302: the browser keeps the original URL so go_router
# can still read the route it was asked for.
/*    /index.html    200
